                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_601">Worcester,
                            Worcestershire, Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the
                            Virgin</orgName> <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition
                            of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in
                            the Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                            Britain index card was originally written by Ker in black pen. It gives
                            the following reason for a potential attribution: 'Worcester calendar:
                            Wulfstan (2 feasts), Oswald ep. (2 feasts), Egwin; July 9 Obitus Ri. de
                            Aumbrisley (s.xiv)'. However, Ker later returned to this card and
                            reassessed the evidence, adding another note (this time in pencil):
                            'Should be rejected: Sir Ivor Atkins writes "The music of the hymns
                            alone would show it to be non-wig ... moreover the form of the melodies
                            is all wrong for Wig."</p></provenance>
                    </history>
